  "body": "Web Animations does not define the element context or timing needed to\nresolve relative lengths in rangeStart or rangeEnd. CSSWG resolved that\nstring and Typed OM inputs accept only absolute lengths and percentages\nuntil an evaluation model is specified.\n\nBlink has accepted relative lengths for some time, so changing this\nbehavior directly could break sites. Gate standards-compliant rejection\nbehind an experimental runtime feature, preserve legacy behavior\notherwise, and record whether affected inputs are accepted or rejected.\nThis lets WPT exercise the new behavior while compatibility data is\ncollected before it is enabled by default.\n\nValidate both input forms consistently, accept absolute Typed OM lengths,\nremove obsolete WPT baselines, expand WPT coverage, and add unit coverage\nfor both runtime-feature states and histogram outcomes.\n\nCSSWG resolution:\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13853\n\nBug: 546237331\nChange-Id: Ifa11dcb9977ea52c55e18c265a5b6c2b0f8ef8d4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8255374\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \\<kevers@chromium.org>\nCommit-Queue: Nicolás Peña \\<npm@chromium.org>\nReviewed-by: Nicolás Peña \\<npm@chromium.org>\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1685690}\n\n",
